{:en {:title "Native selfhost status: a reproducible compiler, C performance still ahead"
:description "12 October 2026 checkpoint: native seed fixed point, bounded byte-tree lowering, exploratory C comparisons and remaining gates. Optimization goal paused."
:intro "The native seed compiler reproduces itself byte for byte across three generations. The latest generic lookup-table lowering improves two exploratory timings and reduces their artifacts. The goal of matching or beating C across Embench is still unmet; this campaign is paused at the user’s request."
:notice "Snapshot: 2026-10-12. Source snapshot f86c2a6f06e55d77b22a574ac91df59590212cdc and its restart package are now published on the preservation branch (checkpoint 3eace60393ac711da7f243d72cca813cbe911fef). This historical snapshot is not a release or the current main compiler. Safety-fixed reintegration was merged to main in PR #1291: the historical 16-module source remains independent of the current main optimizer. Both check and compile refuse explicit policy, including missing policy values. Production and trusted bootstrap loaders are separately source-bound and fuzz-qualified. All final CI and review threads passed before merge. Both compiler closures have three byte-identical generations, 34 policy refusals each and 19 unchanged native images. The current resume pins are linked below; no performance search was restarted. Timings below are exploratory observations, not official Embench scores or statistically established speedups."
:sections [{:title "What was implemented"
:paragraphs ["The native seed backend lowers a closed, typed, pure and uncharged i64-to-i64 threshold tree to an immutable byte lookup table. Leaves must fit 0–255, positive thresholds are bounded by 4095 and depth by 12. Signed negative and high inputs take the original default paths before reading the table. The production matcher does not name benchmarks."
"The optimizer keeps type, owner, label, ABI, effect, trap, fuel and allocation-budget conditions. Compiler token capacity was raised from 393216 to 524288 records with corresponding internal layout changes: compiler model allocation grows by 4 MiB. Guest ABI, guest fuel and loader limits are unchanged. An earlier token-fit claim omitted the library appended before lexing; that claim was withdrawn and failed attempts retained."]}
{:title "Exploratory comparison with C"
:paragraphs ["One local AArch64 macOS C/OFF/ON trio per workload, n=32, calls=64, warm=1; metric BATCH_ABI_RESET_VALIDATION_V1. These are body-time observations, not official Embench scores. No fresh all-19 timing comparison or precision repeats were completed for this candidate. Lower time is better; ON/C above 1 means slower than C."]
