:paragraphs-after ["Native image bytes: PicoJPEG 59412 → 50924 (−8488); QRduino 33272 → 25712 (−7560). Earlier small positive experiments were also recovered into the local ancestry. Their differing baselines cannot be added together or presented as a current aggregate Embench score."]}
{:title "What the qualification establishes"
:paragraphs ["The same full 16-module seed source rebuilt G2, G3 and G4 with identical native images and KSEED containers. G4 native: 1680776 bytes, SHA-256 00ae06cc5ec4cb549780850d3a075f4da22fe09a4de7cd5ed1106bdf1c2e674d. Container: 1680803 bytes, SHA-256 47f60249ca67c2b81f7a7f1eaf30160f66a6c7a02f326ab4454a7cdca68c6328."
"All 19 original benchmark sources compiled and extracted successfully. Only PicoJPEG and QRduino changed; the other 17 native images, containers and exports were byte-identical. The selected 95 functional rows comprise 10 freshly executed canonical profiles (0, 1, 2, 17, 32 for each changed workload) and 85 reused rows justified by exact artifact identity. Results, fuel and arena observations were checked."
"Independent source, machine-code, fixed-point and qualification reviews passed. Tracked bootstrap binaries remained unchanged. Compilation success and reused correctness evidence are distinct from fresh execution or performance measurement of every workload."]}
{:title "Selfhost scope and remaining work"
:paragraphs ["This fixed point covers the native seed compiler route producing KSEED. It does not establish equivalence to the ordinary typed-KIR/provenance KEXE path, or 100% selfhosting of all product check/compile/refactor entry points. The public bin/amu remains a Node launcher."
"C performance across the original 19 workloads remains an open goal. Fresh full-suite timing, product-path qualification and whole-product qualification remain separate work; safety-fixed preservation source has been integrated. Current main has a separately integrated seed. The safety-fixed historical closure is preserved separately, retaining the current optimizer and production loader; both closures have correctness-only native qualification. This does not constitute a new performance measurement. General GP2/Sea-of-Nodes rewriting, verified ComputeCID → ResultCID analysis reuse, iGPU/Neural Engine use and int4/int8 optimization are design or separate qualification topics; this campaign does not prove they are implemented or responsible for these speedups."
"Definition CIDs identify content. A future computation key can include implementation, input state, dependency closure, rewrite rules, ABI, effect/trap and resource contracts; cached results must replay downstream state contributions. CID equality alone does not prove semantic preservation."
"The optimization goal and its agents are paused. Proposed ordinary-call lookup transfer and constructor optimizations remain unadopted. Resume from the qualified local snapshot only after a new instruction."]}]
